# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar Belakang {#background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial demonstrates how to implement the Krylov quantum diagonalization (KQD) algorithm within the context of Qiskit patterns.\n"
"You will first learn the theory behind the algorithm and then see a demonstration of its execution on a QPU.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini mendemonstrasikan cara mengimplementasikan diagonalisasi kuantum Krylov (KQD) dalam konteks pola Qiskit. Kamu akan mempelajari teori di balik algoritma ini terlebih dahulu, lalu melihat demonstrasi eksekusinya di QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Estimating the low-energy properties of many-body Hamiltonians is a central task in quantum simulation.\n"
"For example, ground-state energies and low-lying excitations are directly related to chemical stability, magnetic ordering, quantum phase transitions, and material response.\n"
"On a classical computer, the Hilbert-space dimension grows exponentially with the number of orbitals or spins, so direct diagonalization quickly becomes impractical.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengestimasi sifat energi rendah dari Hamiltonian banyak-benda adalah tugas utama dalam simulasi kuantum.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, energi keadaan dasar dan eksitasi tingkat rendah berkaitan langsung dengan stabilitas kimia, tata magnetik, transisi fase kuantum, dan respons material.\n"
"Pada komputer klasik, dimensi ruang Hilbert tumbuh secara eksponensial seiring bertambahnya jumlah orbital atau spin, sehingga diagonalisasi langsung dengan cepat menjadi tidak praktis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are several quantum-computing approaches to this problem.\n"
"Near-term variational methods, such as the [variational quantum eigensolver (VQE)](/tutorials/spin-chain-vqe), use relatively shallow parameterized circuits, but they require a nonlinear classical optimization loop with many quantum-circuit evaluations.\n"
"At the other end, [quantum phase estimation (QPE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0604193) provides a more direct route to eigenvalue estimation with rigorous guarantees, but standard QPE requires long coherent circuits and is mainly suited to fault-tolerant quantum computers.\n"
"KQD sits between these two approaches: it uses real-time Hamiltonian evolution, as in phase-estimation-based algorithms, but replaces full phase estimation with a compact projected eigenvalue problem that can be solved classically.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada beberapa pendekatan komputasi kuantum untuk masalah ini.\n"
"Metode variasional jangka pendek, seperti [variational quantum eigensolver (VQE)](/tutorials/spin-chain-vqe), menggunakan circuit berparameter yang relatif dangkal, tetapi memerlukan loop optimasi klasik nonlinear dengan banyak evaluasi quantum circuit.\n"
"Di sisi lain, [quantum phase estimation (QPE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0604193) memberikan rute yang lebih langsung untuk estimasi eigenvalue dengan jaminan yang ketat, tetapi QPE standar memerlukan circuit koheren yang panjang dan terutama cocok untuk komputer kuantum fault-tolerant.\n"
"KQD berada di antara kedua pendekatan ini: ia menggunakan evolusi Hamiltonian real-time, seperti pada algoritma berbasis phase-estimation, tetapi menggantikan phase estimation penuh dengan masalah eigenvalue terproyeksi yang ringkas yang bisa diselesaikan secara klasik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider an $n$-qubit Hamiltonian $H$ and a reference state $\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
"The KQD method builds a Krylov subspace from real-time evolved states,\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan Hamiltonian $n$-qubit $H$ dan keadaan referensi $\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
"Metode KQD membangun subruang Krylov dari keadaan yang berevolusi secara real-time,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle = e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t H}\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\ell = 0,1,\\ldots,r-1,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle = e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t H}\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\ell = 0,1,\\ldots,r-1,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $r$ is the Krylov dimension and $\\Delta t$ is the time step.\n"
"Any state in the Krylov subspace is then represented as a linear combination of these basis states,\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $r$ adalah dimensi Krylov dan $\\Delta t$ adalah langkah waktu.\n"
"Setiap keadaan dalam subruang Krylov kemudian direpresentasikan sebagai kombinasi linear dari keadaan basis ini,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi(\\mathbf{c})\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi(\\mathbf{c})\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle}\n"
"{\\left\\|\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle\\right\\|},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where the denominator normalizes the state.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle}\n"
"{\\left\\|\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle\\right\\|},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where the denominator normalizes the state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With simple algebra, we can see that the corresponding energy is written as the Rayleigh quotient,\n"
msgstr "Dengan aljabar sederhana, kita bisa melihat bahwa energi yang bersesuaian ditulis sebagai Rayleigh quotient,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"E(\\mathbf{c})\n"
"=\\langle \\psi(\\mathbf{c})|H|\\psi(\\mathbf{c}) \\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"E(\\mathbf{c})\n"
"=\\langle \\psi(\\mathbf{c})|H|\\psi(\\mathbf{c}) \\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, the matrices $\\mathcal{S}$ and $\\mathcal{H}$,\n"
msgstr "Di sini, matriks $\\mathcal{S}$ dan $\\mathcal{H}$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"define the projected overlap and Hamiltonian matrices.\n"
"Their entries are estimated using quantum-circuit measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"mendefinisikan matriks overlap dan Hamiltonian yang diproyeksikan.\n"
"Entrinya diestimasi menggunakan pengukuran quantum circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We aim to find the coefficient $\\mathbf{c}$ that gives the minimum $E(\\mathbf{c})$:\n"
msgstr "Kita bertujuan menemukan koefisien $\\mathbf{c}$ yang menghasilkan $E(\\mathbf{c})$ minimum:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\min_{\\mathbf{c}\\neq \\mathbf{0}} E(\\mathbf{c}).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\min_{\\mathbf{c}\\neq \\mathbf{0}} E(\\mathbf{c}).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By the Rayleigh-Ritz theorem, this minimization is equivalent to solving the generalized eigenvalue problem (GEVP),\n"
msgstr "Menurut teorema Rayleigh-Ritz, minimisasi ini setara dengan menyelesaikan generalized eigenvalue problem (GEVP),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}=E \\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}=E \\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the dimension $r$ can be small enough for a classical computer to solve the GEVP.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa dimensi $r$ bisa cukup kecil sehingga komputer klasik bisa menyelesaikan GEVP.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the same variational principle used in classical subspace diagonalization, but here the basis states are generated by quantum time evolution.\n"
"Compared with VQE, KQD usually requires deeper circuits because it relies on real-time evolution.\n"
"In return, KQD avoids nonlinear parameter optimization and iterative quantum-hardware execution, and it systematically improves as the projected subspace is enlarged.\n"
"The algorithm has been demonstrated at large scale on existing quantum hardware [\\[2\\]](#references), and its performance can be analyzed with provable guarantees [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah prinsip variasional yang sama yang digunakan dalam diagonalisasi subruang klasik, tetapi di sini keadaan basisnya dihasilkan oleh evolusi waktu kuantum.\n"
"Dibandingkan dengan VQE, KQD biasanya memerlukan circuit yang lebih dalam karena bergantung pada evolusi real-time.\n"
"Sebagai imbalannya, KQD menghindari optimasi parameter nonlinear dan eksekusi perangkat keras kuantum iteratif, dan secara sistematis meningkat seiring diperbesarnya subruang yang diproyeksikan.\n"
"Algoritma ini telah didemonstrasikan dalam skala besar pada perangkat keras kuantum yang ada [\\[2\\]](#references), dan kinerjanya bisa dianalisis dengan jaminan yang bisa dibuktikan [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

