# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian and reference state {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"
msgstr "Hamiltonian dan keadaan referensi {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses a 12-qubit open-boundary Heisenberg chain ($n=12$),\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini menggunakan rantai Heisenberg batas terbuka 12-qubit ($n=12$),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with a single-excitation product state\n"
msgstr "dengan keadaan produk eksitasi tunggal\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"as the reference state.\n"
"Because the Heisenberg Hamiltonian defined above conserves the total number of excitations, the reference state stays in the single-excitation subspace, whose dimension grows only linearly with the number of qubits. We can therefore compute the exact ground-state energy efficiently, by diagonalizing the Hamiltonian restricted to that subspace, and use it purely as a diagnostic benchmark for the KQD estimate. The KQD workflow itself estimates projected matrix elements by using Qiskit primitives and solves the resulting projected problem classically.\n"
msgstr ""
"sebagai keadaan referensi.\n"
"Karena Hamiltonian Heisenberg yang didefinisikan di atas mengonservasi jumlah total eksitasi, keadaan referensi tetap berada dalam subruang eksitasi tunggal, yang dimensinya hanya bertumbuh secara linear terhadap jumlah qubit. Oleh karena itu, kita dapat menghitung energi keadaan dasar yang eksak secara efisien, dengan mendiagonalisasi Hamiltonian yang dibatasi pada subruang tersebut, dan menggunakannya murni sebagai benchmark diagnostik untuk estimasi KQD. Alur kerja KQD sendiri mengestimasi elemen matriks terproyeksi dengan menggunakan Qiskit primitives dan menyelesaikan masalah terproyeksi yang dihasilkan secara klasik.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the parameters for the algorithm {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"
msgstr "Atur parameter untuk algoritma {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Based on the upper-bounds on the Hamiltonian norm, Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) heuristically suggests the time step $\\Delta t$ as $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Because the spectral norm $\\|H\\|$ is hard to compute, we instead use its upper bound:\n"
msgstr ""
"Berdasarkan batas atas pada norma Hamiltonian, Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) secara heuristik menyarankan langkah waktu $\\Delta t$ sebagai $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Karena norma spektral $\\|H\\|$ sulit dihitung, kita malah menggunakan batas atasnya:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We set the Krylov dimension to $r=10$ and the number of Trotter steps per time step to $5$: a large enough Krylov space to resolve the low-lying spectrum while keeping the deepest circuit ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$) affordable, and enough Trotter steps to keep the discretization error small at that deepest circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kita menetapkan dimensi Krylov ke $r=10$ dan jumlah langkah Trotter per langkah waktu ke $5$: ruang Krylov yang cukup besar untuk menyelesaikan spektrum berenergi rendah sambil menjaga circuit terdalam ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$) tetap terjangkau, dan langkah Trotter yang cukup untuk menjaga error diskretisasi tetap kecil pada circuit terdalam tersebut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build circuit {#build-circuit}"
msgstr "Membangun circuit {#build-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we build the circuits to estimate the matrix elements $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ and $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Because all powers of $H$ commute, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita membangun circuit untuk mengestimasi elemen matriks $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ dan $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Karena semua pangkat dari $H$ berkomutasi, kita memperoleh\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we present the circuit, called **extended-swap-test**, which prepares\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita menyajikan circuit, yang disebut **extended-swap-test**, yang menyiapkan\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"di mana $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference state {#reference-state}"
msgstr "Keadaan referensi {#reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare the reference state $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Kita menyiapkan keadaan referensi $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time evolution {#time-evolution}"
msgstr "Evolusi waktu {#time-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Realize the time-evolution operator generated by the Hamiltonian, approximated by simple [Lie-Trotterization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter).\n"
msgstr "Realisasikan operator evolusi waktu yang dihasilkan oleh Hamiltonian, diaproksimasi dengan [Lie-Trotterization sederhana](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extended swap test circuit [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"
msgstr "Circuit extended swap test [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first prepares the reference state on the system register while the ancilla remains in $|0\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "Circuit pertama-tama menyiapkan keadaan referensi pada register sistem sementara ancilla tetap berada di $|0\\rangle$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then, applying a Hadamard gate to the ancilla creates a coherent superposition of two branches:\n"
msgstr "Kemudian, menerapkan gate Hadamard pada ancilla menciptakan superposisi koheren dari dua cabang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, the controlled time-evolution gate applies:\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya, gate evolusi waktu terkontrol diterapkan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "only when the ancilla is in the $|1\\rangle$ branch. Therefore,\n"
msgstr "hanya ketika ancilla berada di cabang $|1\\rangle$. Oleh karena itu,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next code block, we implement:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"which will be assigned as $t=d\\Delta t$ for $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ in the execution step.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada blok kode berikutnya, kita mengimplementasikan:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"yang akan ditetapkan sebagai $t=d\\Delta t$ untuk $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ pada langkah eksekusi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observables {#observables}"
msgstr "Observable {#observables}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For any Hermitian system observable $O$, here we set the observables to calculate:\n"
msgstr "Untuk observable sistem Hermitian $O$ apa pun, di sini kita menetapkan observable yang akan dihitung:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is because $O=I$ gives the overlap element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, while $O=H$ gives the Hamiltonian element $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Ini karena $O=I$ memberikan elemen overlap $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, sementara $O=H$ memberikan elemen Hamiltonian $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, we have\n"
msgstr "Dengan menggunakan $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, kita memperoleh\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, using $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"
msgstr "Demikian pula, dengan menggunakan $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh karena itu, kita memperoleh\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, for each state $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, we need to measure:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, untuk setiap keadaan $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, kita perlu mengukur:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ untuk } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ untuk } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ untuk } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ untuk } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the estimation of the $\\mathcal{H}$ matrix elements, the number of Pauli terms is much larger than that for the $\\mathcal{S}$ matrix elements.\n"
msgstr "Untuk estimasi elemen matriks $\\mathcal{H}$, jumlah suku Pauli jauh lebih besar dibandingkan untuk elemen matriks $\\mathcal{S}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now reduce the number of measured Hamiltonian terms by using a shifting technique [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"We split the Hamiltonian as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang dapat mengurangi jumlah suku Hamiltonian yang diukur dengan menggunakan teknik pergeseran [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"Kita memisahkan Hamiltonian sebagai:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $T$ is chosen such that the reference state is its eigenstate,\n"
msgstr "di mana $T$ dipilih sedemikian rupa sehingga keadaan referensi merupakan eigenstate-nya,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then,\n"
msgstr "Then,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here,\n"
msgstr "Here,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is the shifted Hamiltonian matrix element.\n"
"Therefore, we only need to measure $X\\otimes (H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"The contribution from $T$ is reconstructed classically using the already measured overlap matrix element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"adalah elemen matriks Hamiltonian yang telah digeser.\n"
"Oleh karena itu, kita hanya perlu mengukur $X\\otimes (H-T)$ dan $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"Kontribusi dari $T$ direkonstruksi secara klasik dengan menggunakan elemen matriks overlap $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ yang telah diukur.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, a natural choice is the diagonal part of the Heisenberg Hamiltonian,\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh ini, pilihan yang alami adalah bagian diagonal dari Hamiltonian Heisenberg,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the reference state is a computational-basis state, it is an eigenstate of every $Z_iZ_{i+1}$ term.\n"
msgstr "Karena keadaan referensi adalah keadaan basis komputasi, ia merupakan eigenstate dari setiap suku $Z_iZ_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, a more advantageous choice is to include not only the diagonal $ZZ$ terms, but also the $XX+YY$ terms that annihilate the reference state.\n"
msgstr "Namun, pilihan yang lebih menguntungkan adalah menyertakan tidak hanya suku diagonal $ZZ$, tetapi juga suku $XX+YY$ yang menganihilasi keadaan referensi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each neighboring pair, the operator $XX+YY$ satisfies\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap pasangan tetangga, operator $XX+YY$ memenuhi\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "and\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, the $XX+YY$ term contributes only when the two neighboring qubits have different occupations in the reference bitstring.\n"
"If the two qubits are both $0$ or both $1$, the term annihilates the reference state and can also be shifted out.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh karena itu, suku $XX+YY$ berkontribusi hanya ketika dua qubit tetangga memiliki okupansi yang berbeda pada bitstring referensi.\n"
"Jika kedua qubit sama-sama $0$ atau sama-sama $1$, suku tersebut menganihilasi keadaan referensi dan juga dapat digeser keluar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, where $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Thus, we can choose\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, di mana $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Dengan demikian, kita dapat memilih\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This operator still satisfies\n"
msgstr "Operator ini masih memenuhi\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"because the $ZZ$ terms act diagonally on $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, while the shifted $XX+YY$ terms give zero.\n"
"The corresponding eigenvalue is therefore determined only by the $ZZ$ terms,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"karena suku $ZZ$ bekerja secara diagonal pada $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, sementara suku $XX+YY$ yang telah digeser memberikan nol.\n"
"Eigenvalue yang bersesuaian oleh karena itu ditentukan hanya oleh suku $ZZ$,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this choice, the shifted Hamiltonian becomes:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan pilihan ini, Hamiltonian yang telah digeser menjadi:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a result, only the edges with different occupations in the reference state need to be measured.\n"
"All $ZZ$ terms and all inactive $XX+YY$ terms are reconstructed through the overlap contribution $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, or give zero contribution by construction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai hasilnya, hanya edge dengan okupansi yang berbeda pada keadaan referensi yang perlu diukur.\n"
"Semua suku $ZZ$ dan semua suku $XX+YY$ yang tidak aktif direkonstruksi melalui kontribusi overlap $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, atau memberikan kontribusi nol berdasarkan konstruksinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives a smaller observable than shifting only the diagonal part.\n"
"In particular, for a computational-basis reference state with a localized excitation, only the edges adjacent to the excitation remain in $H-T$.\n"
"Therefore, the number of Pauli terms in $X\\otimes(H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ can be substantially reduced, while the reconstructed matrix element\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini menghasilkan observable yang lebih kecil dibandingkan hanya menggeser bagian diagonal.\n"
"Secara khusus, untuk keadaan referensi basis komputasi dengan eksitasi yang terlokalisasi, hanya edge yang berdekatan dengan eksitasi yang tersisa dalam $H-T$.\n"
"Oleh karena itu, jumlah suku Pauli dalam $X\\otimes(H-T)$ dan $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ dapat dikurangi secara substansial, sementara elemen matriks yang direkonstruksi\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "remains exactly the same.\n"
msgstr "tetap sama persis.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi perangkat keras kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we turn the abstract extended-swap-test circuit into a hardware-oriented template.\n"
"Before that, we further optimize the circuit in the abstract level first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita mengubah circuit extended-swap-test yang abstrak menjadi template yang berorientasi hardware.\n"
"Sebelum itu, kita terlebih dahulu mengoptimalkan lebih lanjut circuit tersebut pada level abstrak.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare Hamiltonian term ordering {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"
msgstr "Membandingkan urutan suku Hamiltonian {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we compare different orderings of the Pauli terms in the Heisenberg Hamiltonian for the Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
"The Hamiltonian itself is unchanged, but the ordering affects how the product-formula circuit is generated and how much the structure can be parallelized in the circuit.\n"
"For example, the naive ordering lists all nearest-neighbor $XX$ terms, then all $YY$ terms, then all $ZZ$ terms.\n"
"This places adjacent edges such as $(0,1)$ and $(1,2)$ next to each other, so they cannot be executed in parallel.\n"
"The even-then-odd ordering visits disjoint even edges first, followed by odd edges, which exposes parallel two-qubit layers.\n"
"The even-odd edge-grouped ordering goes one step further: for each edge, it keeps the local $XX$, $YY$, and $ZZ$ terms together, while still visiting even edges before odd edges.\n"
"We expect the even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings to reduce circuit depth by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, and the edge-grouped ordering to additionally reduce the Trotter error because the local two-qubit interaction on the same edge is handled as a compact block.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, kita membandingkan berbagai urutan suku Pauli dalam Hamiltonian Heisenberg untuk simulasi Hamiltonian.\n"
"Hamiltonian itu sendiri tidak berubah, tetapi urutan tersebut memengaruhi bagaimana circuit product-formula dihasilkan dan seberapa besar strukturnya dapat diparalelkan dalam circuit.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, urutan naif mendaftarkan semua suku $XX$ tetangga terdekat, kemudian semua suku $YY$, lalu semua suku $ZZ$.\n"
"Hal ini menempatkan edge yang berdekatan seperti $(0,1)$ dan $(1,2)$ bersebelahan satu sama lain, sehingga tidak dapat dieksekusi secara paralel.\n"
"Urutan even-then-odd mengunjungi edge genap yang saling lepas terlebih dahulu, diikuti oleh edge ganjil, yang menyingkap layer dua-qubit paralel.\n"
"Urutan even-odd edge-grouped melangkah lebih jauh lagi: untuk setiap edge, ia menjaga suku $XX$, $YY$, dan $ZZ$ lokal tetap bersama, sambil tetap mengunjungi edge genap sebelum edge ganjil.\n"
"Kita mengharapkan urutan even-then-odd dan even-odd edge-grouped mengurangi kedalaman circuit dengan menyingkap layer dua-qubit paralel, dan urutan edge-grouped juga mengurangi error Trotter karena interaksi dua-qubit lokal pada edge yang sama ditangani sebagai blok yang kompak.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Hamiltonian ordering also affects the Trotter error.\n"
"If we place noncommuting terms next to each other, the basis transitions occur more often, which induces more Trotter error.\n"
"By grouping terms that require the same Pauli-basis transformation, redundant basis-changes can be avoided.\n"
msgstr ""
"Urutan Hamiltonian juga memengaruhi error Trotter.\n"
"Jika kita menempatkan suku-suku yang tidak berkomutasi bersebelahan, transisi basis terjadi lebih sering, yang menyebabkan lebih banyak error Trotter.\n"
"Dengan mengelompokkan suku-suku yang memerlukan transformasi basis-Pauli yang sama, perubahan basis yang redundan dapat dihindari.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the comparison uses the largest evolution time that appears in the first-row Krylov estimates,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"using the same transpilation condition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, perbandingan menggunakan waktu evolusi terbesar yang muncul dalam estimasi Krylov baris pertama,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"dengan menggunakan kondisi transpilasi yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to measure the Trotter error, we use **process infidelity** between the Trotterized circuit and the exact Hamiltonian evolution,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengukur error Trotter, kita menggunakan **process infidelity** antara circuit yang di-Trotterisasi dan evolusi Hamiltonian yang eksak,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"
msgstr ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This diagnostic uses dense matrices, so it is suitable for this small 12-qubit example but not intended as a scalable subroutine.\n"
msgstr "Diagnostik ini menggunakan matriks padat, sehingga cocok untuk contoh 12-qubit kecil ini tetapi tidak dimaksudkan sebagai subrutin yang scalable.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We first keep the synthesis rule fixed to one first-order Trotter step and vary only the Pauli-term ordering.\n"
"The goal of this comparison is mainly to see how much circuit depth and two-qubit cost can be reduced by exposing disjoint nearest-neighbor edges to the transpiler.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita terlebih dahulu menjaga aturan sintesis tetap pada satu langkah Trotter orde pertama dan hanya memvariasikan urutan suku Pauli.\n"
"Tujuan dari perbandingan ini terutama untuk melihat seberapa besar kedalaman circuit dan biaya dua-qubit dapat dikurangi dengan menyingkap edge tetangga terdekat yang saling lepas kepada transpiler.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At `reps=1`, we observe that even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings both collapse the depth from 15 to 6 by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, while the two-qubit gate count stays the same across all three orderings.\n"
"However, all three orderings have infidelity close to 1, so we sweep the number of Trotter repetitions to separate the orderings more clearly.\n"
"As the number of repetitions grows, the infidelity of `even-odd edge-grouped` ordering drops faster than the other two, reaching 0.045 at `reps=8` versus 0.075 for naive and even-then-odd ordering.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada `reps=1`, kita mengamati bahwa urutan even-then-odd dan even-odd edge-grouped keduanya mengempiskan kedalaman dari 15 menjadi 6 dengan menyingkap layer dua-qubit paralel, sementara jumlah gate dua-qubit tetap sama di ketiga urutan tersebut.\n"
"Namun, ketiga urutan tersebut memiliki infidelity mendekati 1, sehingga kita menyapu jumlah repetisi Trotter untuk memisahkan urutan-urutan tersebut secara lebih jelas.\n"
"Seiring bertambahnya jumlah repetisi, infidelity dari urutan `even-odd edge-grouped` turun lebih cepat dibandingkan dua urutan lainnya, mencapai 0.045 pada `reps=8` dibandingkan 0.075 untuk urutan naif dan even-then-odd.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare product-formula synthesis {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"
msgstr "Membandingkan sintesis product-formula {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we explore different advanced settings of Trotterization, with the fixed Hamiltonian ordering to the even-odd edge-grouped ordering.\n"
"We consider first-order Lie-Trotter, second-order Suzuki-Trotter, and fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, kita mengeksplorasi berbagai pengaturan lanjutan dari Trotterization, dengan urutan Hamiltonian tetap pada urutan even-odd edge-grouped.\n"
"Kita mempertimbangkan Lie-Trotter orde pertama, Suzuki-Trotter orde kedua, dan Suzuki-Trotter orde keempat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lie-Trotter gives the shallowest circuit but has the largest error, while the fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter is more accurate but increases the circuit depth.\n"
"For the rest of the tutorial, we choose second-order Suzuki-Trotter because it gives a small-depth circuit while substantially reducing the Trotter error relative to the first-order formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lie-Trotter memberikan circuit yang paling dangkal tetapi memiliki error terbesar, sementara Suzuki-Trotter orde keempat lebih akurat tetapi meningkatkan kedalaman circuit.\n"
"Untuk sisa tutorial ini, kita memilih Suzuki-Trotter orde kedua karena memberikan circuit berkedalaman kecil sambil secara substansial mengurangi error Trotter relatif terhadap formula orde pertama.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove the controlled time-evolution gate {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"
msgstr "Menghapus gate evolusi waktu terkontrol {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the extended swap test, controlling time evolution with a single ancilla qubit requires the ancilla to control many gates across the system.\n"
"This can introduce substantial routing overhead and, in the worst case, effectively requires all-to-one connectivity.\n"
"To avoid this, further optimization is possible by replacing the controlled time-evolution gate with a control-free version, exploiting the symmetry of the Hamiltonian.\n"
"Let's observe the following circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam extended swap test, mengontrol evolusi waktu dengan satu qubit ancilla mengharuskan ancilla untuk mengontrol banyak gate di seluruh sistem.\n"
"Hal ini dapat memperkenalkan overhead routing yang substansial dan, dalam kasus terburuk, secara efektif memerlukan konektivitas all-to-one.\n"
"Untuk menghindari hal ini, optimasi lebih lanjut dimungkinkan dengan menggantikan gate evolusi waktu terkontrol dengan versi bebas-kontrol, memanfaatkan simetri Hamiltonian.\n"
"Mari kita amati circuit berikut.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"
msgstr "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $B_{\\rm ref}$ prepares the reference state, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, $B_{\\rm ref}$ menyiapkan keadaan referensi, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of first preparing $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ and then applying $U(t)$ only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch, the circuit directly prepares the two branches as\n"
msgstr "Alih-alih terlebih dahulu menyiapkan $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ dan kemudian menerapkan $U(t)$ hanya pada cabang $|1\\rangle$, circuit secara langsung menyiapkan kedua cabang sebagai\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where\n"
msgstr "where\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first applies a Hadamard gate to the ancilla and prepares the reference state only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch:\n"
msgstr "Circuit pertama-tama menerapkan gate Hadamard pada ancilla dan menyiapkan keadaan referensi hanya pada cabang $|1\\rangle$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then the uncontrolled time-evolution operator is applied to both branches:\n"
msgstr "Kemudian operator evolusi waktu yang tidak terkontrol diterapkan pada kedua cabang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the Hamiltonian preserves the excitation number, we can see that $|0^n\\rangle$ is its eigenstate, and thus\n"
"the evolution operator only accumulates a phase under the Hamiltonian:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena Hamiltonian mempertahankan jumlah eksitasi, kita dapat melihat bahwa $|0^n\\rangle$ adalah eigenstate-nya, dan dengan demikian\n"
"operator evolusi hanya mengakumulasi fase di bawah Hamiltonian:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore,\n"
msgstr "Therefore,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, $B_{\\rm ref}$ is applied only on the $|0\\rangle$ branch.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, $B_{\\rm ref}$ diterapkan hanya pada cabang $|0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this point, the two branches have an extra relative phase. To remove it, we apply the ancilla phase gate\n"
msgstr "Pada titik ini, kedua cabang memiliki fase relatif tambahan. Untuk menghilangkannya, kita menerapkan gate fase ancilla\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This transforms the state as\n"
msgstr "Ini mentransformasi keadaan sebagai\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, up to an irrelevant global phase, we finally prepared\n"
msgstr "Dengan demikian, hingga fase global yang tidak relevan, kita akhirnya menyiapkan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the next code block, we implement this control-free circuit.\n"
msgstr "Pada blok kode berikutnya, kita mengimplementasikan circuit bebas-kontrol ini.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/790e5e0c-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/790e5e0c-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation {#transpilation}"
msgstr "Transpilasi {#transpilation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, we transpile the controlled- and control-free circuits to become executable on the hardware.\n"
"Let's compare the result of the transpiled circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, kita mentranspilasi circuit terkontrol dan bebas-kontrol agar dapat dieksekusi pada hardware.\n"
"Mari kita bandingkan hasil dari circuit yang telah ditranspilasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next step is to submit the same parameterized circuit for several values of $d$. For each $d$, we estimate four expectation values: $X\\otimes I$, $Y\\otimes I$, $X\\otimes (H-T)$, and $Y\\otimes (H-T)$. These four numbers are then combined into the complex first-row elements $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ and $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}$.\n"
msgstr "Langkah selanjutnya adalah mengirimkan circuit terparameterisasi yang sama untuk beberapa nilai $d$. Untuk setiap $d$, kita mengestimasi empat nilai ekspektasi: $X\\otimes I$, $Y\\otimes I$, $X\\otimes (H-T)$, dan $Y\\otimes (H-T)$. Keempat angka ini kemudian digabungkan menjadi elemen baris pertama kompleks $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ dan $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $\\mathcal{S}_{00}=1$ and $\\mathcal{H}_{00}=\\langle\\psi_{0}|(H-T)|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_{0}|H|\\psi_{0}\\rangle-\\tau$ can be classically calculated since $\\lvert\\psi_0\\rangle$ is sparse, so we skip the $d=0$ case.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, $\\mathcal{S}_{00}=1$ dan $\\mathcal{H}_{00}=\\langle\\psi_{0}|(H-T)|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_{0}|H|\\psi_{0}\\rangle-\\tau$ dapat dihitung secara klasik karena $\\lvert\\psi_0\\rangle$ bersifat sparse, sehingga kita melewatkan kasus $d=0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After estimating the projected matrices, we regularize and solve the GEVP\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c} = E\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"The smallest generalized eigenvalue gives the KQD estimate of the ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah mengestimasi matriks yang terproyeksi, kita meregularisasi dan menyelesaikan GEVP\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c} = E\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Eigenvalue tergeneralisasi terkecil memberikan estimasi KQD dari energi keadaan dasar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we solve the generalized eigenvalue problem using the matrices reconstructed from the circuit estimates.\n"
"In an ideal statevector calculation with exact real-time evolution, this should reproduce the exact projected result.\n"
"In practice, deviations can come from Trotterization, sampling error, and numerical instability of the overlap matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita menyelesaikan masalah eigenvalue tergeneralisasi dengan menggunakan matriks yang direkonstruksi dari estimasi circuit.\n"
"Dalam perhitungan statevector yang ideal dengan evolusi waktu-nyata yang eksak, ini seharusnya mereproduksi hasil terproyeksi yang eksak.\n"
"Dalam praktiknya, deviasi dapat berasal dari Trotterization, error sampling, dan ketidakstabilan numerik dari matriks overlap.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We observe how the energy converges as we increase the dimension of the Krylov subspace.\n"
msgstr "Kita mengamati bagaimana energi konvergen seiring kita meningkatkan dimensi subruang Krylov.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/08d57f33-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/08d57f33-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh hardware skala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous section used a 12-qubit model so that the statevector simulation could be used as a diagnostic. We now scale the same KQD workflow to a 30-qubit Heisenberg chain and prepare the workload for execution on IBM Quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Bagian sebelumnya menggunakan model 12-qubit sehingga simulasi statevector dapat digunakan sebagai diagnostik. Sekarang kita menskalakan alur kerja KQD yang sama ke rantai Heisenberg 30-qubit dan menyiapkan workload untuk eksekusi pada hardware IBM Quantum.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1-4 compressed into a single code block {#steps-1-4-compressed-into-a-single-code-block}"
msgstr "Langkah 1-4 dipadatkan menjadi satu blok kode {#steps-1-4-compressed-into-a-single-code-block}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we now put all of these details together into a singular workflow at a larger scale, which is then run on our real quantum hardware. In this section, we apply realistic error-mitigation settings to improve the reliability of the results. Since the matrix elements corresponding to different values of $d$ can be evaluated in parallel, we use `Batch` mode to execute them efficiently.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita sekarang menggabungkan semua detail ini menjadi satu alur kerja tunggal pada skala yang lebih besar, yang kemudian dijalankan pada hardware kuantum nyata kita. Pada bagian ini, kita menerapkan pengaturan mitigasi error yang realistis untuk meningkatkan keandalan hasil. Karena elemen matriks yang bersesuaian dengan nilai $d$ yang berbeda dapat dievaluasi secara paralel, kita menggunakan mode `Batch` untuk mengeksekusinya secara efisien.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/e3e0d1f3-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/e3e0d1f3-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix: The Hamiltonian-function (spectral-filter) viewpoint {#appendix-the-hamiltonian-function-spectral-filter-viewpoint}"
msgstr "Lampiran: Sudut pandang fungsi-Hamiltonian (filter-spektral) {#appendix-the-hamiltonian-function-spectral-filter-viewpoint}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The main workflow presented KQD operationally: build a Krylov basis from real-time-evolved states, estimate the projected matrices $\\mathcal{H}$ and $\\mathcal{S}$, and solve the GEVP.\n"
"This appendix revisits the *same* computation from a complementary angle that explains **why** KQD works: the *Hamiltonian-function*, or *spectral-filter*, viewpoint [\\[3\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references).\n"
"It reuses the 12-qubit model, time step $\\Delta t$, and the Krylov solution already obtained above; no new circuit execution is required.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alur kerja utama menyajikan KQD secara operasional: membangun basis Krylov dari keadaan yang dievolusikan secara waktu-nyata, mengestimasi matriks terproyeksi $\\mathcal{H}$ dan $\\mathcal{S}$, dan menyelesaikan GEVP.\n"
"Lampiran ini meninjau kembali perhitungan yang *sama* dari sudut pandang komplementer yang menjelaskan **mengapa** KQD bekerja: sudut pandang *fungsi-Hamiltonian*, atau *filter-spektral* [\\[3\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references).\n"
"Lampiran ini menggunakan kembali model 12-qubit, langkah waktu $\\Delta t$, dan solusi Krylov yang sudah diperoleh di atas; tidak diperlukan eksekusi circuit baru.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference state as an energy distribution {#the-reference-state-as-an-energy-distribution}"
msgstr "Keadaan referensi sebagai distribusi energi {#the-reference-state-as-an-energy-distribution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the Hamiltonian have the eigendecomposition\n"
msgstr "Misalkan Hamiltonian memiliki dekomposisi eigen\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{m} E_m\\,|E_m\\rangle\\!\\langle E_m|,\n"
"\\qquad E_0\\le E_1\\le\\cdots,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{m} E_m\\,|E_m\\rangle\\!\\langle E_m|,\n"
"\\qquad E_0\\le E_1\\le\\cdots,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"with energy eigenstates $|E_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Any reference state can be expanded in this eigenbasis,\n"
msgstr ""
"dengan eigenstate energi $|E_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Keadaan referensi apa pun dapat diekspansikan dalam basis eigen ini,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\sum_m a_m\\,|E_m\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad a_m=\\langle E_m|\\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\sum_m a_m\\,|E_m\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad a_m=\\langle E_m|\\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"so it carries a **spectral weight** $p_m=|a_m|^2$ at each energy $E_m$.\n"
"The reference energy is the mean of this distribution, $\\langle H\\rangle_{0}=\\sum_m p_m E_m$.\n"
msgstr ""
"sehingga ia membawa **bobot spektral** $p_m=|a_m|^2$ pada setiap energi $E_m$.\n"
"Energi referensi adalah rata-rata dari distribusi ini, $\\langle H\\rangle_{0}=\\sum_m p_m E_m$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The eigendecomposition of a general $n$-qubit Hamiltonian is exponentially costly, so this picture is only a diagnostic, which is *not* part of the algorithm.\n"
"Here, however, we can compute it cheaply for the *same* $n=12$ problem: the Heisenberg Hamiltonian conserves the total excitation number, and the reference $|000001000000\\rangle$ carries a single excitation, so its entire spectral content lives in the single-excitation subspace whose dimension grows only linearly with $n$.\n"
"We therefore reuse the exact single-excitation block (already used above as a benchmark) and read off the reference distribution $\\{(E_m, p_m)\\}$ inside that subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dekomposisi eigen dari Hamiltonian $n$-qubit yang umum berbiaya eksponensial, sehingga gambaran ini hanya merupakan diagnostik, yang *bukan* bagian dari algoritma.\n"
"Di sini, bagaimanapun, kita dapat menghitungnya dengan murah untuk masalah $n=12$ yang *sama*: Hamiltonian Heisenberg mengonservasi jumlah total eksitasi, dan referensi $|000001000000\\rangle$ membawa satu eksitasi, sehingga seluruh konten spektralnya berada dalam subruang eksitasi tunggal yang dimensinya hanya bertumbuh secara linear terhadap $n$.\n"
"Oleh karena itu, kita menggunakan kembali blok eksitasi tunggal yang eksak (sudah digunakan di atas sebagai benchmark) dan membaca distribusi referensi $\\{(E_m, p_m)\\}$ di dalam subruang tersebut.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "KQD learns a filter that reshapes this distribution {#kqd-learns-a-filter-that-reshapes-this-distribution}"
msgstr "KQD mempelajari filter yang membentuk ulang distribusi ini {#kqd-learns-a-filter-that-reshapes-this-distribution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **Hamiltonian function** $f(H)$ is defined through spectral calculus,\n"
msgstr "Sebuah **fungsi-Hamiltonian** $f(H)$ didefinisikan melalui kalkulus spektral,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f(H)=\\sum_m f(E_m)\\,|E_m\\rangle\\!\\langle E_m|,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f(H)=\\sum_m f(E_m)\\,|E_m\\rangle\\!\\langle E_m|,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"or in other words, a weighted sum of eigenprojectors.\n"
"Applying it to the reference reshapes each spectral amplitude, $a_m \\to a_m f(E_m)$:\n"
msgstr ""
"atau dengan kata lain, jumlah berbobot dari eigenprojector.\n"
"Menerapkannya pada referensi membentuk ulang setiap amplitudo spektral, $a_m \\to a_m f(E_m)$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f(H)\\,|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\sum_m a_m\\,f(E_m)\\,|E_m\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f(H)\\,|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\sum_m a_m\\,f(E_m)\\,|E_m\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $f$ were sharply peaked at the lowest energy ($f(E_0)=1$ and $f(E_m)\\approx 0$ otherwise) then $f(H)$ would act as a ground-state projector, and the normalized output would be (close to) the ground state.\n"
"Therefore, a good low-pass **spectral filter** in energy is exactly what we want.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $f$ memiliki puncak yang tajam pada energi terendah ($f(E_0)=1$ dan $f(E_m)\\approx 0$ selainnya) maka $f(H)$ akan bertindak sebagai proyektor keadaan-dasar, dan output yang dinormalisasi akan (mendekati) keadaan dasar.\n"
"Oleh karena itu, **filter spektral** low-pass yang baik dalam energi adalah tepat apa yang kita inginkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "KQD does not prescribe $f$ in advance. Instead it expands the filter in the real-time-evolution basis,\n"
msgstr "KQD tidak menentukan $f$ terlebih dahulu. Sebaliknya, ia mengekspansikan filter dalam basis evolusi waktu-nyata,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f_{\\rm KQD}(E)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell\\, e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t E},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f_{\\rm KQD}(E)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell\\, e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t E},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"a *trigonometric* function of the energy whose coefficients $\\{c_\\ell\\}$ are precisely the GEVP eigenvector solved for above.\n"
"Minimizing the Rayleigh quotient $\\mathbf{c}^\\dagger\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}/\\mathbf{c}^\\dagger\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}$ is therefore the same as *learning* the filter that best suppresses the excited-state weight of the reference.\n"
"Larger Krylov dimension $r$ gives the filter more degrees of freedom and a sharper peak at the ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"sebuah fungsi *trigonometrik* dari energi yang koefisiennya $\\{c_\\ell\\}$ tepatnya merupakan eigenvector GEVP yang diselesaikan di atas.\n"
"Meminimalkan quotient Rayleigh $\\mathbf{c}^\\dagger\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}/\\mathbf{c}^\\dagger\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}$ oleh karena itu sama dengan *mempelajari* filter yang paling baik menekan bobot keadaan-tereksitasi dari referensi.\n"
"Dimensi Krylov $r$ yang lebih besar memberikan filter lebih banyak derajat kebebasan dan puncak yang lebih tajam pada energi keadaan-dasar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The helper below evaluates this learned filter on an energy axis; we then apply it to the reference distribution obtained above.\n"
msgstr "Helper di bawah ini mengevaluasi filter yang telah dipelajari ini pada sumbu energi; kita kemudian menerapkannya pada distribusi referensi yang diperoleh di atas.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the filter and its flexibility {#visualize-the-filter-and-its-flexibility}"
msgstr "Memvisualisasikan filter dan fleksibilitasnya {#visualize-the-filter-and-its-flexibility}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We first show the learned filter at the full Krylov dimension used above, then track how it sharpens as the dimension $r$ grows.\n"
msgstr "Kita pertama-tama menunjukkan filter yang telah dipelajari pada dimensi Krylov penuh yang digunakan di atas, kemudian melacak bagaimana filter tersebut menajam seiring bertambahnya dimensi $r$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bars show the reference spectral weights $p_m$ (before) and the filtered weights $p_m|f_{\\rm KQD}(E_m)|^2$ (after), together with the learned filter intensity $|f_{\\rm KQD}(E)|^2$ on a continuous energy axis.\n"
"The filter concentrates the weight onto the lowest energy of the single-excitation subspace &mdash; the same energy that the KQD estimate converged to in the small-scale example.\n"
"Note that this is the ground state *within the single-excitation sector*, which is the relevant target for this excitation-conserving reference state, not the global ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Batang menunjukkan bobot spektral referensi $p_m$ (sebelum) dan bobot yang telah difilter $p_m|f_{\\rm KQD}(E_m)|^2$ (sesudah), bersama dengan intensitas filter yang telah dipelajari $|f_{\\rm KQD}(E)|^2$ pada sumbu energi kontinu.\n"
"Filter memusatkan bobot pada energi terendah dari subruang eksitasi tunggal &mdash; energi yang sama dengan tempat estimasi KQD berkonvergensi pada contoh skala kecil.\n"
"Perhatikan bahwa ini adalah keadaan dasar *dalam sektor eksitasi tunggal*, yang merupakan target yang relevan untuk keadaan referensi yang mengonservasi eksitasi ini, bukan keadaan dasar global.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/app-code-plot-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/app-code-plot-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Increasing the Krylov dimension: flexibility of the learned function {#increasing-the-krylov-dimension-flexibility-of-the-learned-function}"
msgstr "Meningkatkan dimensi Krylov: fleksibilitas dari fungsi yang telah dipelajari {#increasing-the-krylov-dimension-flexibility-of-the-learned-function}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recall that the learned filter is a trigonometric polynomial in the energy with $r$ coefficients,\n"
msgstr "Ingat kembali bahwa filter yang telah dipelajari adalah polinomial trigonometrik dalam energi dengan $r$ koefisien,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f_{\\rm KQD}(E)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell\\, e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t E}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"f_{\\rm KQD}(E)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell\\, e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t E}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Krylov dimension $r$ is exactly the number of free coefficients, so it controls the **flexibility** of the function.\n"
"A small $r$ can only produce a broad, gently varying filter that leaks weight into low-lying excited states; when $r$ increases, the filter can form a narrower peak at the target energy and suppress the remaining excited-state weight more aggressively.\n"
"This is the spectral-filter counterpart of the energy convergence observed in the small-scale example: as $r$ grows, the filtered distribution collapses onto the subspace ground state and the estimated energy decreases toward it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dimensi Krylov $r$ persis merupakan jumlah koefisien bebas, sehingga ia mengontrol **fleksibilitas** dari fungsi tersebut.\n"
"$r$ yang kecil hanya dapat menghasilkan filter yang lebar dan bervariasi secara perlahan yang membocorkan bobot ke keadaan-keadaan tereksitasi berenergi rendah; ketika $r$ meningkat, filter dapat membentuk puncak yang lebih sempit pada energi target dan menekan sisa bobot keadaan-tereksitasi secara lebih agresif.\n"
"Ini adalah rekan filter-spektral dari konvergensi energi yang diamati pada contoh skala kecil: seiring bertambahnya $r$, distribusi yang telah difilter mengempis menuju keadaan dasar subruang dan energi yang diestimasi menurun mendekatinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We reuse the projected matrices already estimated above and simply solve the GEVP at each leading $r\\times r$ block, then evaluate and plot the corresponding filter.\n"
msgstr "Kita menggunakan kembali matriks terproyeksi yang sudah diestimasi di atas dan cukup menyelesaikan GEVP pada setiap blok $r\\times r$ terdepan, kemudian mengevaluasi dan memplot filter yang bersesuaian.\n"

